# Client Code Quality

Condensed from `client/CLAUDE.md`. Keep in sync when either changes.

## Stack — current idioms only

React 19 · TS (strict) · Vite 8 · Tailwind v4 · TanStack Query v5 · Zustand v5 ·
react-hook-form v7 + Zod v4 · react-router v7 · socket.io-client v4 · dayjs ·
shared fetch client (`shared/lib/api/client`).

- Server data → TanStack Query. **Never** `useState`+`useEffect`+fetch for API data.
- Client/UI/session state → Zustand (selectors; no server data inside).
- Forms → react-hook-form + Zod schemas in the feature (`authValidators`-style field
  `validate` / schema helpers). Schema is source of truth; prefer `z.infer`. Do not
  invent a second validation stack.
- `useEffect` only for external systems (DOM/socket/subscriptions); always clean up.
- Realtime → `useSocketEvent` + `shared/constants/socket.ts`; handlers update Query
  cache/stores, not local copies.
- Function components + hooks only. No class components, deprecated APIs, or `any`.
- Do not add paid analytics/Sentry without TECH.md approval.

## Errors & toasts

- Query / load errors → `useErrors` (`shared/hooks/useError`).
- Mutations that need a loading toast → `useAsyncMutation`.
- One-off UX validation messages → `toast.*` in a **hook** (not deep leaf UI, not pages).
- Avoid double-toasting the same failure.

## Env

Allowlist only: `VITE_BASE_URL`, `VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` (public; may be unset → feature no-ops).
Every `VITE_*` must be declared on `ImportMetaEnv` in `vite-env.d.ts`. No secrets in `VITE_*`.
Cookies only (`credentials: 'include'`); no access tokens in `localStorage`.
No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` for user content.

## CSS homes

- App tokens / `@theme` / shared utilities → root entry CSS (`index.css` today). **Do not
  keep appending** large feature blobs here — extract or colocate.
- Landing-only tokens/classes (`lw-*`) → `styles/landing.css` only.
- One-off composites → small colocated CSS next to the component (e.g. carousel).
- Don't add new rules to legacy `App.css` without consolidating into the homes above.

## DRY — single source of truth

**Search before you write** — reuse or extend, never paste a second copy.

- Types / constants / logic / UI: one home; extract at ≥2 usages.
- Re-export from old path when relocating to avoid wide sweeps.
- Judgment: one source per concept — equal-today-but-different-reasons ≠ duplication.

## Quality bar

- **≤ 350 lines/file.** Over → split.
- No `console.*`, commented-out code, dead code, or unused exports.
- A11y: semantic HTML, keyboard controls, `aria-label` on icon buttons, `aria-hidden`
  on decorative SVGs, visible focus, honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Path alias `@/` for cross-layer imports; relative only within a feature/folder.
- Naming: Components PascalCase; hooks `useX`; utils camelCase; scalars SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE; folders kebab-case.
- Before done: `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` must pass.

## Performance

- Virtualize long chat/message lists.
- Subscribe to narrow Zustand slices.
- Keep admin/chart code in lazy routes / manual chunks.
- Mutations invalidate precise query keys; socket handlers update Query *or* Zustand for a given fact — not both.
